{"answer": "The GitHub REST API returns a JSON body and has the base URL https://api.github.com.", "trace": {"request_id": "2f693f0c9f2a4534", "formation": "auto", "source": "auto", "dispatch": {"stage_id": "dispatch", "kind": "dispatch", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "deepseek", "wire_model": "openai/deepseek-v4-flash", "api_base": "https://api.deepseek.com/v1", "prompt": "User's request:\nName one real-world API that returns a JSON body and give its base URL. One sentence.", "response": "{\n  \"formation\": {\n    \"stages\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"worker_1\",\n        \"kind\": \"worker\",\n        \"model\": \"openrouter/openai/gpt-5.6-luna\",\n        \"depends_on\": [],\n        \"progressive\": false,\n        \"wait_messages\": [],\n        \"trigger\": \"\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"worker_2\",\n        \"kind\": \"worker\",\n        \"model\": \"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro\",\n        \"depends_on\": [],\n        \"progressive\": false,\n        \"wait_messages\": [],\n        \"trigger\": \"\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"aggregator\",\n        \"kind\": \"aggregator\",\n        \"model\": \"openrouter/qwen/qwen3.7-plus\",\n        \"depends_on\": [\n          \"worker_1\",\n          \"worker_2\"\n        ],\n        \"progressive\": false,\n        \"wait_messages\": [],\n        \"trigger\": \"\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"edges\": [\n      [\n        \"worker_1\",\n        \"aggregator\"\n      ],\n      [\n        \"worker_2\",\n        \"aggregator\"\n      ]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"worker_prompts\": [\n    {\n      \"stage_id\": \"worker_1\",\n      \"model\": \"openrouter/openai/gpt-5.6-luna\",\n      \"prompt\": \"List 3 well-known public web APIs that return a JSON response body (not XML/HTML), and for each give its exact base URL (scheme + host, e.g. https://api.example.com). For each, state in one short clause what the base URL serves and confirm that responses are JSON with an application/json content type. Order the list by how confidently you can vouch for the base URL being correct and currently live. Do not write prose beyond the numbered list.\",\n      \"expected_output_schema\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"stage_id\": \"worker_2\",\n      \"model\": \"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Act as a technical fact-checker on API endpoints. Independently propose 3 real, publicly documented HTTP APIs that return JSON. For each, give: (a) the base URL, (b) a concrete example path appended to it, (c) the HTTP method, and (d) one sentence on why you are confident the base URL is correct and the payload is JSON. Then flag any candidate that is a documentation site rather than an API host, any that returns non-JSON by default, and any whose base URL is commonly misquoted. Output as a numbered list plus a short 'flags' section.\",\n      \"expected_output_schema\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"aggregator_instructions\": \"Worker 1 (gpt-5.6-luna) produced a ranked list of 3 public JSON APIs with base URLs, ordered by confidence, with a JSON-content-type note for each. Worker 2 (deepseek-v4-pro) independently produced 3 candidate APIs with base URL, example path, HTTP method, a confidence sentence, and a 'flags' section marking documentation-site lookalikes, non-JSON-by-default services, and commonly misquoted base URLs. Merge: (1) take the intersection/overlap of the two lists first — any API both workers named is the safest choice; (2) if there is no overlap, prefer a Worker 1 candidate whose base URL is not contradicted by Worker 2's flags, and drop anything Worker 2 flagged as a docs site, non-JSON, or a misquoted URL; (3) then answer the user's question with exactly ONE sentence that names the single API and gives its literal base URL — nothing else, no preamble, no list, no explanation of candidates considered. The sentence must be grammatically complete, must contain the base URL as a plain string (e.g. https://api.github.com), and must not hedge with words like 'many', 'such as', or 'for example'. Disagreements between workers are resolved silently in favor of the unflagged, overlapping candidate; do not mention the deliberation in the final sentence.\",\n  \"stage_instructions\": {\n    \"aggregator\": \"Resolve conflicts by preferring candidates both workers independently named and that carry no flag from Worker 2. Emit only the final one-sentence answer naming one real API and its base URL.\"\n  },\n  \"output_schema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"answer\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"description\": \"The final merged answer for the user: one sentence naming one real-world JSON API and its base URL.\"\n      },\n      \"sources\": {\n        \"type\": \"array\",\n        \"items\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"description\": \"Worker IDs that contributed\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"required\": [\n      \"answer\"\n    ]\n  }\n}", "tokens_input": 19884, "tokens_output": 1438, "latency_ms": 12470, "cost": 0.0038453999999999997, "depends_on": [], "iteration": 1, "started_at": 222353.39982986, "ended_at": 222365.870638491, "finish_reason": "stop", "negotiated_format": {"requested": "json_object", "served": null}, "ranked_candidates": [], "rank_kappa": null, "rank_model": "", "rank_tokens_input": 0, "rank_tokens_output": 0, "rank_cost": 0.0, "rank_error": null, "degraded": false, "fallback_attempts": []}, "workers": [{"stage_id": "worker_1", "kind": "worker", "model": "openrouter/openai/gpt-5.6-luna", "provider": "openrouter", "wire_model": "openrouter/openai/gpt-5.6-luna", "api_base": "", "prompt": "## User request\nName one real-world API that returns a JSON body and give its base URL. One sentence.\n\n## Your assigned task\nList 3 well-known public web APIs that return a JSON response body (not XML/HTML), and for each give its exact base URL (scheme + host, e.g. https://api.example.com). For each, state in one short clause what the base URL serves and confirm that responses are JSON with an application/json content type. Order the list by how confidently you can vouch for the base URL being correct and currently live. Do not write prose beyond the numbered list.", "response": "1. **GitHub REST API** — `https://api.github.com` serves GitHub resources, with responses returned as JSON using `application/json`.\n2. **Open-Meteo API** — `https://api.open-meteo.com` serves weather forecasts, with responses returned as JSON using `application/json`.\n3. **JSONPlaceholder API** — `https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com` serves mock REST resources, with responses returned as JSON using `application/json`.", "tokens_input": 131, "tokens_output": 382, "latency_ms": 6594, "cost": 0.00012529999999999998, "depends_on": [], "iteration": 1, "started_at": 222365.872208047, "ended_at": 222372.46674, "finish_reason": "stop", "negotiated_format": null, "ranked_candidates": [], "rank_kappa": null, "rank_model": "", "rank_tokens_input": 0, "rank_tokens_output": 0, "rank_cost": 0.0, "rank_error": null, "degraded": false, "fallback_attempts": []}, {"stage_id": "worker_2", "kind": "worker", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro", "provider": "deepseek", "wire_model": "openai/deepseek-v4-pro", "api_base": "https://api.deepseek.com/v1", "prompt": "## User request\nName one real-world API that returns a JSON body and give its base URL. One sentence.\n\n## Your assigned task\nAct as a technical fact-checker on API endpoints. Independently propose 3 real, publicly documented HTTP APIs that return JSON. For each, give: (a) the base URL, (b) a concrete example path appended to it, (c) the HTTP method, and (d) one sentence on why you are confident the base URL is correct and the payload is JSON. Then flag any candidate that is a documentation site rather than an API host, any that returns non-JSON by default, and any whose base URL is commonly misquoted. Output as a numbered list plus a short 'flags' section.", "response": "One example: GitHub REST API, base URL `https://api.github.com`.\n\n1. **GitHub REST API**  \n   (a) Base URL: `https://api.github.com`  \n   (b) Example path: `/users/octocat`  \n   (c) Method: `GET`  \n   (d) GitHub’s official REST documentation uses `https://api.github.com` as the API host, and `GET /users/octocat` returns JSON with `Content-Type: application/json`.\n\n2. **OpenWeatherMap Current Weather API**  \n   (a) Base URL: `https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5`  \n   (b) Example path: `/weather?q=London&appid=YOUR_API_KEY`  \n   (c) Method: `GET`  \n   (d) OpenWeatherMap’s documented endpoint is under this host/path, and it defaults to JSON unless `mode` is set to XML or HTML.\n\n3. **REST Countries API**  \n   (a) Base URL: `https://restcountries.com/v3.1`  \n   (b) Example path: `/name/usa`  \n   (c) Method: `GET`  \n   (d) The REST Countries docs specify this base URL, and `/name/usa` returns a JSON array of matching country objects.\n\n**Flags**  \n- None of the listed base URLs are documentation sites; each is an API host.  \n- None of these listed endpoints return non-JSON by default.  \n- OpenWeatherMap’s base URL is commonly misquoted as `https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather`, but that is an endpoint path, not the base URL.  \n- REST Countries is commonly misquoted by its old base URL `https://restcountries.eu`; the current base URL is `https://restcountries.com/v3.1`.", "tokens_input": 237, "tokens_output": 3987, "latency_ms": 63877, "cost": 0.008050680000000001, "depends_on": [], "iteration": 1, "started_at": 222365.872577121, "ended_at": 222429.749764272, "finish_reason": "stop", "negotiated_format": null, "ranked_candidates": [], "rank_kappa": null, "rank_model": "", "rank_tokens_input": 0, "rank_tokens_output": 0, "rank_cost": 0.0, "rank_error": null, "degraded": false, "fallback_attempts": []}], "aggregator": {"stage_id": "aggregator", "kind": "aggregator", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "provider": "deepseek", "wire_model": "openai/deepseek-v4-flash", "api_base": "https://api.deepseek.com/v1", "prompt": "merge stage 'aggregator' over upstream: worker_1, worker_2", "response": "{\"answer\":\"The GitHub REST API returns a JSON body and has the base URL https://api.github.com.\",\"sources\":[\"worker_1\",\"worker_2\"]}", "tokens_input": 1020, "tokens_output": 135, "latency_ms": 1320, "cost": 0.000234, "depends_on": ["worker_1", "worker_2"], "iteration": 1, "started_at": 222429.750063036, "ended_at": 222431.070787088, "finish_reason": "stop", "negotiated_format": {"requested": "json_schema", "served": null}, "ranked_candidates": [], "rank_kappa": null, "rank_model": "", "rank_tokens_input": 0, "rank_tokens_output": 0, "rank_cost": 0.0, "rank_error": null, "degraded": false, "fallback_attempts": []}, "stages": [{"stage_id": "worker_1", "kind": "worker", "model": "openrouter/openai/gpt-5.6-luna", "provider": "openrouter", "wire_model": "openrouter/openai/gpt-5.6-luna", "api_base": "", "prompt": "## User request\nName one real-world API that returns a JSON body and give its base URL. One sentence.\n\n## Your assigned task\nList 3 well-known public web APIs that return a JSON response body (not XML/HTML), and for each give its exact base URL (scheme + host, e.g. https://api.example.com). For each, state in one short clause what the base URL serves and confirm that responses are JSON with an application/json content type. Order the list by how confidently you can vouch for the base URL being correct and currently live. Do not write prose beyond the numbered list.", "response": "1. **GitHub REST API** — `https://api.github.com` serves GitHub resources, with responses returned as JSON using `application/json`.\n2. **Open-Meteo API** — `https://api.open-meteo.com` serves weather forecasts, with responses returned as JSON using `application/json`.\n3. **JSONPlaceholder API** — `https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com` serves mock REST resources, with responses returned as JSON using `application/json`.", "tokens_i